  {"heading":"Basic syntax and structure / Sintaxe e estrutura básicas","segment_index":"S8.P10","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/writing_functions.qmd:190-191","tr_span":"chapters/writing_functions.pt.qmd:189-189","proposition":"The English says the anonymous function selects every second observation of the dataset; the Portuguese says it selects the second record of the dataset (\"selecionar o segundo registro\"), a single row rather than every even-numbered row, which the adjacent chunk `filter(row_number() %%2 == 0)` contradicts.","reader_consequence":"A Portuguese reader believes the modulo filter returns one row (the second observation) and will misread the 10-row output of the chunk, and may reuse `%%2 == 0` expecting a single-record selection.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Testing and Error handling / Teste e tratamento de erros","segment_index":"S18.P3","kind":"code_mismatch","en_span":"chapters/writing_functions.qmd:552-552","tr_span":"chapters/writing_functions.pt.qmd:552-552","proposition":"The English says to run `mean()` and then run it with `safely()`; the Portuguese names the wrapper `secure ()`, a function that does not exist and that does not appear in the adjacent chunk, which calls `safely(mean)`.","reader_consequence":"A Portuguese reader looks for or types `secure()`, gets \"could not find function\", and cannot connect the sentence to the `safe_mean <- safely(mean)` line directly below it.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Modify class of multiple columns in a dataset / Modificar a classe de várias colunas em um conjunto de dados","segment_index":"S12.P2","kind":"code_mismatch","en_span":"chapters/writing_functions.qmd:315-315","tr_span":"chapters/writing_functions.pt.qmd:313-313","proposition":"The English attributes `map_if()` to the **purrr** package; the Portuguese attributes it to the **purr** package, which is not the package used in the adjacent chunk (`purrr::map_if`).","reader_consequence":"A Portuguese reader tries to install or namespace `purr`, which is a different (unrelated) name, instead of `purrr`.","confidence":"medium"}
